## Running the Amazon Experiment

Activate the project virtual environment:

```powershell
cd C:\Users\Wahab\OneDrive\Desktop\FraudSquad-5389
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

Verify the active Python interpreter:

```powershell
python -c "import sys; print(sys.executable)"
```

The interpreter should point to:

```text
FraudSquad-5389\.venv\Scripts\python.exe
```

Run the experiment using:

```powershell
python run_detect_amazon.py --device cpu
```

The main experiment uses:

```yaml
max_epochs: 50
device: "cpu"
lm: "bert-base-uncased"
top_ratio: 0.03
```

---

## Experimental Results

The original FraudSquad reproduction produced:

| Metric | Original FraudSquad |
|---|---:|
| AUC | 0.9954 |
| Average Precision | 0.9621 |
| Precision | 0.8621 |
| Recall | 0.9227 |
| F1 | 0.8914 |

After adding the `product_length` relationship:

| Metric | FraudSquad + Product-Length |
|---|---:|
| AUC | **0.9996** |
| Average Precision | **0.9975** |
| Precision | **0.9294** |
| Recall | **0.9947** |
| F1 | **0.9609** |

The modified model improved all five reported metrics.

The largest improvement was observed in recall:

```text
0.9227 → 0.9947
```

The F1-score also increased substantially:

```text
0.8914 → 0.9609
```

These results suggest that product-conditioned review length provides useful additional relational information on the Amazon dataset.

However, the result should not be interpreted as evidence that review length universally improves AI-generated review detection. Generated reviews in this dataset may exhibit length patterns that differ from genuine reviews, so additional cross-domain testing is necessary.

---

## Main Files

```text
run_detect_amazon.py
    Main Amazon experiment and product-length graph extension

preprocess/preprocess.py
    Data preprocessing, BERT embedding generation, graph construction,
    and feature extraction

methods/fraudsquad_src/model_handler.py
    FraudSquad training and evaluation pipeline

config/amazon_cfg_0503.yml
    Amazon experiment configuration

cache/bert_base/
    Saved BERT embedding checkpoints
```

## Summary

The project preserves the original FraudSquad neural architecture while making the implementation easier to reproduce and introducing one additional graph relationship based on review writing length.

The final graph contains:

```text
Original:
user + product_star + product_month

Modified:
user + product_star + product_month + product_length
```

On the Amazon experiment, the modified version increased the final F1-score from approximately 0.89 to 0.96 while achieving approximately 99.5% recall.
